{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Cloud-session guard corpus, ported from red-rostrum#75 (d34b15a) for toast-stats (#2547). Every deny entry must make the PreToolUse guard exit 2 under CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true; every allow entry must exit 0. {{REPO}} is taverns-red/toast-stats and {{BRANCH}} is the session branch checked out in the fixture repo the guard runs in (cloudSessionGuardCorpus.test.ts plants link, homelink, .env, key.pem, notes-private.txt and the rest). Differences from the template: the documented toast-stats worker patterns (gh api POST comments/pulls, PATCH pulls, push -u origin <branch> and HEAD) are allowed; grep -r over the root is denied (it reaches .git and .env); the rest are added cases. writeDeny/writeAllow are repo-relative paths for Write and Edit: the secret-shaped list (read and write) plus config other tools act on (write only); gitlink is a planted symlink to .git. toolDeny/toolAllow are whole hook inputs for the other tools ({{ROOT}} the fixture root, {{HOME}} and {{TMP}} the test process's): Read/Grep/Glob take the Bash read rules; web, MCP and unknown tools are denied; tools without I/O and Agent (its subagents' calls fire PreToolUse too) are allowed; file-tool writes outside the root only under $TMPDIR.",
